%% DM26-0670

%% What identity a credential names, asked before a CSR is made, as built (2026-11-04). user-cert-fetcher is its one caller. polar-init holds its identity itself and does not ask.
%% Unlike /issue, there is no introspection here: it answers for an IdP token signature-checked alone, and issues nothing.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant UserTool as user-cert-fetcher
    participant Obs as Credentials observer<br/>(low trust)
    participant Bk as Cassini broker
    participant Con as Credentials agent<br/>(consumer)
    participant CI as cert-issuer

    Note over UserTool,CI: The client must know the exact identity before it can build a matching CSR,<br/>since the CSR's name has to match before it is ever submitted for signing
    UserTool->>Obs: POST /identity { credential }
    Note over Obs: The route is what makes it this request: the observer does not look inside the credential
    Obs-)Bk: IdentityNormalizationRequest on credentials-identity-normalization-requests,<br/>with a fresh correlation id
    Bk-)Con: delivered, through the request gate, judged as the observer
    Con->>CI: POST /validate { include_normalized_identity: true }
    CI->>CI: validate the token: issuer, signature,<br/>audience, expiry. Then the same<br/>normalize_identity /issue uses,<br/>so the two cannot drift
    CI-->>Con: the identity, or a validation error
    Con-)Bk: Normalized { identity } or Refused { TokenInvalid }, by correlation id
    Bk-)Obs: the reply
    Obs-->>UserTool: the identity, or 401
    Note over UserTool: Next: the CSR, user_cert_issuance_and_usage
